+## Local AMD fixes (7900 XTX, ROCm 7.14, transformers 5)
+- `./run_amd.sh <script>`: runs with the repo venv, `PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1`, no `expandable_segments` (corrupts tensors on ROCm), quiet logging.
+- Models load lazily with a bounded host-RAM cache (`TRELLIS_MODEL_CACHE_GB`, default 5; `TRELLIS_LAZY_LOAD=0` restores eager loading). The full 16 GB checkpoint set no longer gets OOM-killed on a 32 GB host.
+- Lazy models are built directly on the GPU and their weights streamed tensor by tensor (`TRELLIS_LOAD_ON_GPU=0` = old CPU path). The CPU path built each 1.3B DiT in fp32 (~5 GB) plus a full state-dict copy, which got `1024_cascade` killed by the RAM watchdog. Checked bit-identical against the stock loader. `1024_cascade` test: generate 154 s, GLB 29 s, render 17 s, VRAM peak 8.5 GB, RSS peak 12.2 GB.
+- Background removal: `TRELLIS_REMBG=auto|transparent_background|birefnet`. `auto` falls back to transparent-background when the gated RMBG-2.0 cannot be loaded.
+- DINOv3 feature extractor works with transformers 5 (layers moved to `model.model.layer`).
+- EXR environment maps: falls back to the OpenEXR bindings when OpenCV has no OpenEXR support (`render_utils.load_hdri`).
+- nvdiffrast-hip: `patches/nvdiffrast-hip-rocm-fixes.patch` (applied by `setup.sh`) fixes triangles dropped by the rasterizer (speckles in renders and baked textures), depth peeling and a missing `__syncwarp` fence. `NVDR_HIP_VERBOSE=1` re-enables the rasterizer diagnostics.
+- Tests: `tests_amd/` (`test_pipeline.py` end to end; `raster_*.py` rasterizer checks against a brute-force reference).
+
 ## Run app:
 ```bash
 source .venv/bin/activate
 python ./app.py
