+```
+
+## Symmetry (local addition)
+Most generated objects are mirror-symmetric, but the model only produces that approximately.
+`pipeline.run(..., symmetry='auto')` (app: *Symmetry* dropdown, default `auto`) detects mirror
+planes through the grid centre from the stage-1 occupancy and then enforces them without retraining:
+
+1. sparse-structure occupancy logits are averaged with their mirror,
+2. every shape-decoder subdivision decision is averaged with the mirrored child (symmetric voxel set at all levels),
+3. the 7 flexible-dual-grid outputs are mirrored with the exact rule (vertex offset `f -> -f` on the mirror axis,
+   edge flags of the other axes shift one voxel), giving an exactly symmetric mesh,
+4. PBR voxels are averaged with their mirror where both sides agree; strong differences (logos, text) are kept.
+
+`symmetry` also accepts `'off'` (library default) or explicit axes such as `'x'`, `'xy'`; z is up.
+For export, `trellis2.utils.symmetry_glb.to_glb_mirrored` (app: *Mirrored UVs*) unwraps and bakes only one
+half per mirror axis and shares the texture between halves (2x texel area per axis, no seam on the plane).
+It is used only when the texture gate left at most 5% of mirrored voxel pairs asymmetric (otherwise side-specific
+details would be replaced by the mirror of the other side).
+
+Tests: `./run_amd.sh tests_amd/test_symmetry.py` (unit, ~10 s), `tests_amd/test_symmetry_glb.py` (export, ~40 s),
+`tests_amd/sym_calibrate.py` (detection scores for the example images), `tests_amd/sym_compare.py` (off vs auto).
